{"call_id":"call_Dy4K7cUZsBsSzdGmgwBok62l","process_id":"28102","turn_id":"019ca732-e077-79e0-a883-8af70c03460c","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec tasks ready --eligible --json"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec tasks ready --eligible --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"[\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1FCWDDH5FM5JKSWNYVBX\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserv\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserves state. Applies to all list/filter pages (triage, inbox, tasks, etc).\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@web-ui\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.004Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQB2J9SKA1QNC3SG3NN8WF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:17.546Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: Web UI pages lose their filter state when the browser refreshes. For example, filtering tasks by status=in_progress or triage by tag=cli is lost on reload. Filter state should be persisted in URL query parameters so that refreshing preserves the view, and URLs are shareable/bookmarkable.\\n\\n**Where**: The tasks page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/tasks/+page.svelte`) already partially implements URL-based filters — it reads from `$page.url.searchParams` (line 39-47) via the `filterParams` derived value. However, the triage page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) uses local `$state` variables (`filterTag`, `filterStatus` at lines 43-44) that are NOT synced to URL params. Other list pages (items, inbox) likely have the same issue.\\n\\nKey files to update:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte` — filterTag and filterStatus need URL param sync\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/items/+page.svelte` — check if filters use URL params\\n- Any other list/filter pages under `packages/web-ui/src/routes/`\\n\\n**How**: Follow the pattern already established in the tasks page:\\n1. Read initial filter values from `$page.url.searchParams` (from `$app/stores`)\\n2. When a filter changes, use `goto()` (from `$app/navigation`) to update URL params without a full page reload: `goto(\\\\`?status=\\\\${filterStatus}&tag=\\\\${filterTag}\\\\`, { replaceState: true, keepFocus: true })`\\n3. Use `$derived` to compute filter values from URL params (like tasks page does)\\n4. This approach gives: URL persistence, back/forward navigation, shareable links\\n\\nFor the triage page specifically:\\n- Replace `let filterTag = $state('')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('tag')`\\n- Replace `let filterStatus = $state('all')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('status')`\\n- Add `goto()` calls when filters change\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- All list/filter pages read initial state from URL query params\\n- Changing a filter updates the URL without full page reload\\n- Refreshing the page preserves filter state\\n- Browser back/forward navigates between filter states\\n- The triage page URL shows filters like `?status=untriaged&tag=cli`\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWG9550XY4Y8F7V6W5W47\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:48.645Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @web-ui module. URL state persistence for filter/view params across all list pages.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1G6HBSJRXVSWEWQ9W9E4\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, d\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate). Currently no way to filter triage records by action.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@interactive-triage-ui\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.825Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQBJ4QTDMCZJ4NAY7B1KGP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:33.495Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The triage page has status and tag filters (lines 326-347 of `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) but no way to filter triage records by their action type (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate). When reviewing triage history, users often want to see \\\"all promote decisions\\\" or \\\"all spec-gap findings\\\" without scrolling through mixed results.\\n\\n**Where**: `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`:\\n- Existing filters: `filterStatus` (all/untriaged/triaged/acted_on) at line 44, `filterTag` at line 43\\n- Filter UI: lines 324-347 (the filter controls div with data-testid=\\\"triage-filters\\\")\\n- Filtered items computation: `filteredItems` derived at lines 78-96 — currently filters by tag and status only\\n- The `TriageAction` type includes: promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate (defined in `$lib/types/triage`)\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. Add a new `filterAction` state variable: `let filterAction = $state<TriageAction | ''>('')`\\n2. Add a new `<select>` element in the filters div (alongside status and tag filters) with options for each action type\\n3. Add action filtering to the `filteredItems` derived computation:\\n   ```\\n   if (filterAction) {\\n     items = items.filter((i) => i.record?.action === filterAction);\\n   }\\n   ```\\n4. Include the action filter in the `$effect` that resets `currentIndex` when filters change (line 296-302)\\n5. If implementing URL state persistence (task @01KJDQ1F), also sync this filter to URL params\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- A dropdown/select control for triage action type appears in the filter bar\\n- Selecting \\\"promote\\\" shows only items with promote decisions\\n- Selecting \\\"spec-gap\\\" shows only spec-gap items\\n- The empty/default option shows all items (no action filter)\\n- Changing the filter resets the card navigation index to 0\\n- E2E test covers filtering by action type\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWRKV7J9BSC3BY2NNPNG8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:57.179Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @interactive-triage-ui spec. Add filter controls for triage action types on triage page.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation into reconnection logic, heartbeat handling, or fallback to polling.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@daemon-server\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:04.635Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\\n\\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\\n4. **Consider connection health check**: After reconnecting, verify the connection is actually healthy (e.g., send a ping and wait for response) before transitioning to 'connected' state.\\n5. **Investigate MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS**: After 10 failed reconnects, the connection is abandoned permanently. Consider resetting the attempt counter after a successful connection that lasts longer than some threshold (e.g., 60s).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- WebSocket connection remains stable for extended periods without spurious disconnects\\n- Client sends periodic heartbeat/ping to prevent idle timeout\\n- Clean disconnects (code 1000 from client-initiated disconnect) don't trigger reconnection\\n- Console shows clean connection lifecycle without repeated disconnect/reconnect spam\\n- Connection lost indicator (10s threshold) only triggers for genuine server unavailability\\n- Tests cover: heartbeat keeps connection alive, clean close doesn't reconnect, reconnection works after genuine server restart\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQX0Y1T915X3M23D1VS9PP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:48:05.698Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @daemon-server spec (covers WebSocket protocol). Investigate and fix WebSocket reconnection reliability.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGBWNF7Q24AKX2H006YG2RG\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-stale-active-session-cleanup\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Stale Active Session Cleanup\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-stale-cleanup\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-stale-session-candidate-criteria\",\n      \"@implement-auto-abandon-metadata-and-audit-trail\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:15:54.343Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGBWNF783W553MKSVK92XCE\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:15:54.343Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"See plan @plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions for implementation notes\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGCHNSP93AZEXNFGSW9SGBV\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:27:22.807Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Review follow-up: parent task now depends on criteria + metadata tasks to enforce implementation order. Parent task scope is command orchestration + integration tests after dependencies land.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGD47RS0VH81V4AT3R6R76W\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:37:31.033Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Automation triage: eligible. 9 own ACs + 6 traits (43 inherited ACs). Depends on @implement-stale-session-candidate-criteria and @implement-auto-abandon-metadata-and-audit-trail.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  }\n]\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"[\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1FCWDDH5FM5JKSWNYVBX\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserv\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserves state. Applies to all list/filter pages (triage, inbox, tasks, etc).\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@web-ui\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.004Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQB2J9SKA1QNC3SG3NN8WF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:17.546Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: Web UI pages lose their filter state when the browser refreshes. For example, filtering tasks by status=in_progress or triage by tag=cli is lost on reload. Filter state should be persisted in URL query parameters so that refreshing preserves the view, and URLs are shareable/bookmarkable.\\n\\n**Where**: The tasks page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/tasks/+page.svelte`) already partially implements URL-based filters — it reads from `$page.url.searchParams` (line 39-47) via the `filterParams` derived value. However, the triage page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) uses local `$state` variables (`filterTag`, `filterStatus` at lines 43-44) that are NOT synced to URL params. Other list pages (items, inbox) likely have the same issue.\\n\\nKey files to update:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte` — filterTag and filterStatus need URL param sync\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/items/+page.svelte` — check if filters use URL params\\n- Any other list/filter pages under `packages/web-ui/src/routes/`\\n\\n**How**: Follow the pattern already established in the tasks page:\\n1. Read initial filter values from `$page.url.searchParams` (from `$app/stores`)\\n2. When a filter changes, use `goto()` (from `$app/navigation`) to update URL params without a full page reload: `goto(\\\\`?status=\\\\${filterStatus}&tag=\\\\${filterTag}\\\\`, { replaceState: true, keepFocus: true })`\\n3. Use `$derived` to compute filter values from URL params (like tasks page does)\\n4. This approach gives: URL persistence, back/forward navigation, shareable links\\n\\nFor the triage page specifically:\\n- Replace `let filterTag = $state('')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('tag')`\\n- Replace `let filterStatus = $state('all')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('status')`\\n- Add `goto()` calls when filters change\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- All list/filter pages read initial state from URL query params\\n- Changing a filter updates the URL without full page reload\\n- Refreshing the page preserves filter state\\n- Browser back/forward navigates between filter states\\n- The triage page URL shows filters like `?status=untriaged&tag=cli`\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWG9550XY4Y8F7V6W5W47\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:48.645Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @web-ui module. URL state persistence for filter/view params across all list pages.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1G6HBSJRXVSWEWQ9W9E4\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, d\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate). Currently no way to filter triage records by action.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@interactive-triage-ui\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.825Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQBJ4QTDMCZJ4NAY7B1KGP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:33.495Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The triage page has status and tag filters (lines 326-347 of `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) but no way to filter triage records by their action type (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate). When reviewing triage history, users often want to see \\\"all promote decisions\\\" or \\\"all spec-gap findings\\\" without scrolling through mixed results.\\n\\n**Where**: `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`:\\n- Existing filters: `filterStatus` (all/untriaged/triaged/acted_on) at line 44, `filterTag` at line 43\\n- Filter UI: lines 324-347 (the filter controls div with data-testid=\\\"triage-filters\\\")\\n- Filtered items computation: `filteredItems` derived at lines 78-96 — currently filters by tag and status only\\n- The `TriageAction` type includes: promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate (defined in `$lib/types/triage`)\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. Add a new `filterAction` state variable: `let filterAction = $state<TriageAction | ''>('')`\\n2. Add a new `<select>` element in the filters div (alongside status and tag filters) with options for each action type\\n3. Add action filtering to the `filteredItems` derived computation:\\n   ```\\n   if (filterAction) {\\n     items = items.filter((i) => i.record?.action === filterAction);\\n   }\\n   ```\\n4. Include the action filter in the `$effect` that resets `currentIndex` when filters change (line 296-302)\\n5. If implementing URL state persistence (task @01KJDQ1F), also sync this filter to URL params\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- A dropdown/select control for triage action type appears in the filter bar\\n- Selecting \\\"promote\\\" shows only items with promote decisions\\n- Selecting \\\"spec-gap\\\" shows only spec-gap items\\n- The empty/default option shows all items (no action filter)\\n- Changing the filter resets the card navigation index to 0\\n- E2E test covers filtering by action type\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWRKV7J9BSC3BY2NNPNG8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:57.179Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @interactive-triage-ui spec. Add filter controls for triage action types on triage page.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation into reconnection logic, heartbeat handling, or fallback to polling.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@daemon-server\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:04.635Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\\n\\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\\n4. **Consider connection health check**: After reconnecting, verify the connection is actually healthy (e.g., send a ping and wait for response) before transitioning to 'connected' state.\\n5. **Investigate MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS**: After 10 failed reconnects, the connection is abandoned permanently. Consider resetting the attempt counter after a successful connection that lasts longer than some threshold (e.g., 60s).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- WebSocket connection remains stable for extended periods without spurious disconnects\\n- Client sends periodic heartbeat/ping to prevent idle timeout\\n- Clean disconnects (code 1000 from client-initiated disconnect) don't trigger reconnection\\n- Console shows clean connection lifecycle without repeated disconnect/reconnect spam\\n- Connection lost indicator (10s threshold) only triggers for genuine server unavailability\\n- Tests cover: heartbeat keeps connection alive, clean close doesn't reconnect, reconnection works after genuine server restart\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQX0Y1T915X3M23D1VS9PP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:48:05.698Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @daemon-server spec (covers WebSocket protocol). Investigate and fix WebSocket reconnection reliability.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGBWNF7Q24AKX2H006YG2RG\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-stale-active-session-cleanup\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Stale Active Session Cleanup\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-stale-cleanup\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-stale-session-candidate-criteria\",\n      \"@implement-auto-abandon-metadata-and-audit-trail\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:15:54.343Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGBWNF783W553MKSVK92XCE\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:15:54.343Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"See plan @plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions for implementation notes\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGCHNSP93AZEXNFGSW9SGBV\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:27:22.807Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Review follow-up: parent task now depends on criteria + metadata tasks to enforce implementation order. Parent task scope is command orchestration + integration tests after dependencies land.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGD47RS0VH81V4AT3R6R76W\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:37:31.033Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Automation triage: eligible. 9 own ACs + 6 traits (43 inherited ACs). Depends on @implement-stale-session-candidate-criteria and @implement-auto-abandon-metadata-and-audit-trail.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":598788519},"formatted_output":"[\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1FCWDDH5FM5JKSWNYVBX\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserv\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserves state. Applies to all list/filter pages (triage, inbox, tasks, etc).\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@web-ui\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.004Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQB2J9SKA1QNC3SG3NN8WF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:17.546Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: Web UI pages lose their filter state when the browser refreshes. For example, filtering tasks by status=in_progress or triage by tag=cli is lost on reload. Filter state should be persisted in URL query parameters so that refreshing preserves the view, and URLs are shareable/bookmarkable.\\n\\n**Where**: The tasks page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/tasks/+page.svelte`) already partially implements URL-based filters — it reads from `$page.url.searchParams` (line 39-47) via the `filterParams` derived value. However, the triage page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) uses local `$state` variables (`filterTag`, `filterStatus` at lines 43-44) that are NOT synced to URL params. Other list pages (items, inbox) likely have the same issue.\\n\\nKey files to update:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte` — filterTag and filterStatus need URL param sync\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/items/+page.svelte` — check if filters use URL params\\n- Any other list/filter pages under `packages/web-ui/src/routes/`\\n\\n**How**: Follow the pattern already established in the tasks page:\\n1. Read initial filter values from `$page.url.searchParams` (from `$app/stores`)\\n2. When a filter changes, use `goto()` (from `$app/navigation`) to update URL params without a full page reload: `goto(\\\\`?status=\\\\${filterStatus}&tag=\\\\${filterTag}\\\\`, { replaceState: true, keepFocus: true })`\\n3. Use `$derived` to compute filter values from URL params (like tasks page does)\\n4. This approach gives: URL persistence, back/forward navigation, shareable links\\n\\nFor the triage page specifically:\\n- Replace `let filterTag = $state('')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('tag')`\\n- Replace `let filterStatus = $state('all')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('status')`\\n- Add `goto()` calls when filters change\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- All list/filter pages read initial state from URL query params\\n- Changing a filter updates the URL without full page reload\\n- Refreshing the page preserves filter state\\n- Browser back/forward navigates between filter states\\n- The triage page URL shows filters like `?status=untriaged&tag=cli`\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWG9550XY4Y8F7V6W5W47\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:48.645Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @web-ui module. URL state persistence for filter/view params across all list pages.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1G6HBSJRXVSWEWQ9W9E4\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, d\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate). Currently no way to filter triage records by action.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@interactive-triage-ui\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.825Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQBJ4QTDMCZJ4NAY7B1KGP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:33.495Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The triage page has status and tag filters (lines 326-347 of `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) but no way to filter triage records by their action type (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate). When reviewing triage history, users often want to see \\\"all promote decisions\\\" or \\\"all spec-gap findings\\\" without scrolling through mixed results.\\n\\n**Where**: `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`:\\n- Existing filters: `filterStatus` (all/untriaged/triaged/acted_on) at line 44, `filterTag` at line 43\\n- Filter UI: lines 324-347 (the filter controls div with data-testid=\\\"triage-filters\\\")\\n- Filtered items computation: `filteredItems` derived at lines 78-96 — currently filters by tag and status only\\n- The `TriageAction` type includes: promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate (defined in `$lib/types/triage`)\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. Add a new `filterAction` state variable: `let filterAction = $state<TriageAction | ''>('')`\\n2. Add a new `<select>` element in the filters div (alongside status and tag filters) with options for each action type\\n3. Add action filtering to the `filteredItems` derived computation:\\n   ```\\n   if (filterAction) {\\n     items = items.filter((i) => i.record?.action === filterAction);\\n   }\\n   ```\\n4. Include the action filter in the `$effect` that resets `currentIndex` when filters change (line 296-302)\\n5. If implementing URL state persistence (task @01KJDQ1F), also sync this filter to URL params\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- A dropdown/select control for triage action type appears in the filter bar\\n- Selecting \\\"promote\\\" shows only items with promote decisions\\n- Selecting \\\"spec-gap\\\" shows only spec-gap items\\n- The empty/default option shows all items (no action filter)\\n- Changing the filter resets the card navigation index to 0\\n- E2E test covers filtering by action type\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWRKV7J9BSC3BY2NNPNG8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:57.179Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @interactive-triage-ui spec. Add filter controls for triage action types on triage page.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation into reconnection logic, heartbeat handling, or fallback to polling.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@daemon-server\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:04.635Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\\n\\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\\n4. **Consider connection health check**: After reconnecting, verify the connection is actually healthy (e.g., send a ping and wait for response) before transitioning to 'connected' state.\\n5. **Investigate MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS**: After 10 failed reconnects, the connection is abandoned permanently. Consider resetting the attempt counter after a successful connection that lasts longer than some threshold (e.g., 60s).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- WebSocket connection remains stable for extended periods without spurious disconnects\\n- Client sends periodic heartbeat/ping to prevent idle timeout\\n- Clean disconnects (code 1000 from client-initiated disconnect) don't trigger reconnection\\n- Console shows clean connection lifecycle without repeated disconnect/reconnect spam\\n- Connection lost indicator (10s threshold) only triggers for genuine server unavailability\\n- Tests cover: heartbeat keeps connection alive, clean close doesn't reconnect, reconnection works after genuine server restart\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQX0Y1T915X3M23D1VS9PP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:48:05.698Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @daemon-server spec (covers WebSocket protocol). Investigate and fix WebSocket reconnection reliability.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJGBWNF7Q24AKX2H006YG2RG\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-stale-active-session-cleanup\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Stale Active Session Cleanup\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-stale-cleanup\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-stale-session-candidate-criteria\",\n      \"@implement-auto-abandon-metadata-and-audit-trail\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:15:54.343Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGBWNF783W553MKSVK92XCE\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:15:54.343Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"See plan @plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions for implementation notes\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGCHNSP93AZEXNFGSW9SGBV\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:27:22.807Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Review follow-up: parent task now depends on criteria + metadata tasks to enforce implementation order. Parent task scope is command orchestration + integration tests after dependencies land.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJGD47RS0VH81V4AT3R6R76W\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T20:37:31.033Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Automation triage: eligible. 9 own ACs + 6 traits (43 inherited ACs). Depends on @implement-stale-session-candidate-criteria and @implement-auto-abandon-metadata-and-audit-trail.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  }\n]\n","status":"completed"}